          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f11ed3e53b4581c9a88415a4997d3a3c344f7d04",
          "message": "perf(velvet): share one layout computation between the callback refs a commit attaches (#1618)\n\nCloses #1610.\n\nA commit's callback ref, layout effect or imperative handle reads layout only after Velvet applies the panel's pending styles and computes its layout, which it does when the panel root reads as dirty. After each computation Velvet marks the root dirty again. The panel's own layout pass then still runs, still sends GeometryChangedEvents, and still runs before a pick a callback makes. Before this change, a dirty root always meant a new computation. Each ref behind a colour write therefore computed the layout again: N refs cost N computations and N transform walks.\n\nA later read now treats a dirty root as that mark, and skips the computation, only when four things are as the last computation left them:\n\n- the root node's new-layout flag is still set (the panel's own pass clears it on a displayed root);\n- the panel's hierarchy version;\n- the root node's own layout style, compared by `LayoutNode.CopyStyle` against a copy kept on a detached element's node;\n- the dirty flags of the root's direct children.\n\nEach kind of layout change reaches one of them:\n- a change below the root marks its ancestors up to one of those children;\n- a change among the root's own children moves the hierarchy version;\n- a write to the root's own size or style changes that style, including the panel-settings resize.\n\nRefs that each write a colour therefore share one computation within a commit, across a pass's drain, and across the rows a `V.VirtualList` commits one by one. A read behind a write that changes layout computes again. So does a read behind a pass the panel ran since, once the root has been marked dirty again. The gate does not see a change to the layout config's point scale that moves no root size, which the base does not mark either.\n\nAn earlier shape held the root clean across a batch of reads instead. That left a pick made from a callback hit-testing stale boxes, because the engine pass that bumps element sizes and sets display flags never ran. The root is now marked dirty again after each computation, as before.\n\n`RefAttachLayoutCostTests` counts computations for the mount, a pass's drain and five `VirtualList` rows. It also pins each of the four checks:\n- an element added after a computation;\n- a reorder under the root;\n- `PickAll` after an in-place widen, and for a new child outside its parent's box;\n- a ref widening the panel root;\n- a root widened, laid out by the panel, then narrowed back.\n\n`player-builds.md` names the hierarchy version and the layout-style copy among the engine members the reads depend on.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
