          "distinct": true,
          "id": "536780757e9b7c65a4c2d9d375c6d7d975f87bee",
          "message": "test(velvet): answer the 3.0.1 gate's sampled survivors in the reconciler (#1725)\n\nNo issue: this answers the 3.0.1 release gate's sampled mutation survivors in the reconciler's commit, effect, error-boundary, font-scope and z-layer code.\n\nOn main at 7e156844c, the release gate refuses 97 of the 400 mutants it samples, because each one survived and nobody answered for it. This PR answers the 32 in:\n\n- `FiberCommitWork`, `FiberContextSpine`, `FiberEffects`, `FiberElementCleaner`, `FiberErrorBoundary`\n- `FiberFontScope`, `FiberPrimitiveElementPool`, `FiberRenderer`, `FiberWorkLoop`, `FiberZLayerCoordinator`\n- `GeneralPathReconciler`, `Reconciler`, `ReconcilerContext`, `WrapperInfrastructure`\n\n#1723 and #1724 answer the rest.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **25 new cases.** Each asserts state that one of these survivors left unread:\n  - a parked pass's resume on the panel scheduler;\n  - the pass buffers going back to their pools;\n  - a clip-path wrapper's cleanup;\n  - the inherited-font scope's follow and release;\n  - the z-layer hold records;\n  - the error-boundary paths. These are a boundary whose fallback suspends while the failed output still holds a pending completion or a throwing cleanup; a carried catch whose boundary a boundary above replaces; and a boundary whose fallback holds a boundary with a broken fallback.\n\n  Each passes on main and carries a `GREEN_ON_BASE(characterization)` declaration.\n- **6 `MUTANT_SURVIVES` declarations.** These are the only Runtime edits, and they are comments.\n  - **`FiberContextSpine` (2):** the claims are cleared before any read, and the one `PushScope` caller pairs it with `PopScope`.\n  - **`FiberFontScope` (1):** `foreign` is read only for an intent with no family.\n  - **`FiberPrimitiveElementPool` (1):** clearing a childless container takes the early return.\n  - **`GeneralPathReconciler` (1):** every caught-error report goes through `RecordCatch`, which resets `CatchReportedFromCarry` before anything reads it.\n  - **`FiberWorkLoop` (1):** every `ScheduleRerender`/`ScheduleFlush` caller requires a mounted fiber, so the standalone-flush branch is unreachable. The comment that described a fiber \"disposed mid-flight\" there is removed, because no state reaches it.\n\n## Evidence\n\nEach case's kill is traced from the code. The next mutation record run measures them, and this PR's CI measures that every case passes on main. No behaviour changes, so there is no CHANGELOG fragment and no `Documentation~` change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
