          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f7eba2343db75c39637facfb15c0411fc67191e1",
          "message": "fix(velvet): re-apply a host's root setup and its Portal's children to the root a replaced panel rebuilds (#1783)\n\nCloses #1637.\n\nWhen a layer or world-space host's `UIDocument` is disabled across an engine panel update, the engine disposes the panel. Re-enabling it then builds a new root (`UIDocument.RecreateUI`) on a new panel. Velvet left everything it had set up on the old root:\n- the focus navigator, keyed by the old panel;\n- the chained-ring key;\n- the cross-panel event bridge;\n- the default-family hold;\n- the declaring-panel viewport link.\n\nThe Portal's children also stayed on the detached root. The host stayed blank until some unrelated re-render patched the Portal, or for good under `Isolated`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `PanelHostRootWatch` (new, `[ExecuteAlways]`) sits on each host's GameObject. It notices `rootVisualElement` change, waits for the new root's panel, and calls `PanelHostFactory.ApplyRootSetup`. The host creators call the same method, so creation and re-creation apply one setup: declaring root, event bridge, default-family hold, focus navigator and chained-ring key. The old holds are released first.\n- `RenderPortalsInto` asks each Portal on the replaced root to render again. It marks the declaring fiber (`PortalRetargetOwed`), so `ChildReconciler.SkipsIdentical` does not skip a Portal returned by the same instance, as `V.Mount(root, V.Portal(...))` and a Portal passed down as children are. It also marks the range's children pending, so the patch mounts them into the new root.\n- `PatchWorldSpacePre` rebases a world-space range whose recorded target is no longer the host's root, as the layer path already did.\n- Components inside the host mount again, so their state starts over. Keeping it is #1782.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`FocusReplacedHostPanelTests` (PlayMode). Each case folds \"the panel really was replaced\" into its asserted value, so a fixture that kept its panel fails the case rather than passing it. All are red on the base:\n- the navigator on the new panel (Isolated layer, world-space);\n- the chained ring's owner, the event bridge (state and a bubbled pointer event), the default-family hold and the viewport link on the new root;\n- the Portal's children on the new root (in a component, at the root of `V.Mount`, as a re-returned instance, and world-space);\n- the host's class carried;\n- Tab from the host's last focusable returning to the declaring panel (Appended and Chained).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
