          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1e8eebde6b4c0e4b0ac258b3ab8c4480ffd1c173",
          "message": "perf(velvet): read an element's layer map once per class write, and add a mounted theme-scope row benchmark (#1790)\n\nRefs #1651. The per-array class-family mask and the pass gates landed earlier; this adds the pieces that could be done without changing ordering, plus the G4 benchmark. The projection's per-class notify is not batched, so the issue's Done list is not fully met.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `StyleClassProjection.Add`/`Remove` read the element's layer map once for the uniform-scale fallback and the projection, where each class read it twice. Both reads happened before the class was written, with no write between them, so nothing observes the difference.\n- `Runtime/Reconciler/Tests/PlayMode/MountedThemeRowBenchmarks.cs` (G4): styled rows, paint rows and text-size labels mounted through `V.Mount` under a sheet declaring `--color-*`, `--text-*--line-height` and breakpoints. Each sample re-renders a non-memoized component with unchanged class lists.\n\n## Not batched: `NotifyClassesChanged` / `UniformScaleClassFallback`\n\n`DiffClassList` interleaves plain classes (through the projection) with inline-resolved tokens, and `ApplyClassToken` runs the same previous-uniform and scale-fallback refresh itself. A `scale-[..]` token reads scale state that the preceding class's refresh wrote through `ApplyCombinedScale`, and each refresh compares against the uniform scale read before that one class. Running the refresh once after the loop changes what the later token reads, so it is left as is.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `compile_check.py` over every assembly passes; `asset_meta_check.py`, `duplication_check.py` and the refusal baseline diff are clean.\n- No test added: `StyleClassFamiliesTests` already fails when a family's own reading acts on a token whose bit is unset, and `ClassGateThemeScopeTests` pins the scope-dependent families outside the table.\n- No numbers measured locally; the `benchmarks` label's CI data covers `MountedThemeRowBenchmarks`, `Reconcile_UnchangedClassList_100StyledRows`, `PaintPassReconcileBenchmarks`, `TextSizeEffectReconcileBenchmarks` and `VisibleToggleProjectionBenchmarks`.\n- The corpus comparison harness is not in the repository and was not run.\n\nNo `Documentation~` impact; no CHANGELOG fragment (an internal lookup count).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
