          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8e017fa6a02263eb8f44028b607ba07f31b4af3d",
          "message": "ci(velvet): measure the keyed benchmarks on an IL2CPP Linux player by manual dispatch (#1792)\n\nRefs #1669\n\nAdds a manually dispatched workflow, `player-benchmarks.yml`, that builds the keyed PlayMode benchmarks into an IL2CPP StandaloneLinux64 player with the full iteration counts and prints each median to the job summary. It takes `ref` and `filter` inputs, runs on no other event and is not a required check, so it can be dispatched on the commit before and after a change to the props comparer.\n\nThe backend is not committed: an editor-only `ITestPlayerBuildModifier` (`BenchmarkPlayerBuild`) sets IL2CPP, the Release compiler configuration and a `VELVET_BENCHMARK_FULL` scripting define for that build only, where the workflow sets `VELVET_PLAYER_BENCHMARKS=1`. `BenchmarkRun` reads the define, since a player is not handed the editor's command line.\n\n`scripts/ci/player_benchmarks.py` builds the editor command, with unit tests that `test.yml` runs. CONTRIBUTING.md's benchmarks section names the workflow. No CHANGELOG entry: contributor tooling.\n\n## Evidence\n\nA push-triggered copy of this workflow, run on this branch, built the player with IL2CPP: the log runs `il2cpp/build/deploy/UnityLinker`. All 9 `JsFrameworkKeyedBenchmarks` cases passed, with no inconclusive cases, and the medians step wrote the summary (run 44417709115). The base reads `Select_OneOf1000Rows` 7.45 ms / 15,120 GC.Alloc, `Swap_Rows2And999Of1000` 7.76 ms / 15,140 and `Remove_OneOf1000Rows` 8.39 ms / 15,040.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
