          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8aa3e1c36a75d4af03b3e77339562db0e3b41d61",
          "message": "perf(velvet): make sibling Portal mount, hide and reveal cost the same per Portal at 250 and 1,000 (#1719)\n\nCloses #1571. Stacked on #1716.\n\nMounting, hiding and revealing many sibling Portals cost the square of their count. Several steps scanned every Portal, every held range or every sibling once per Portal. Each of those now reads an index.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Hide and reveal.** `GeneralPathReconciler` groups the placed Portals by ancestor once per hide or reveal (`PortalsByAncestor`).\n  - `PortalRangeTable.Resolve` reads positions through `ChildListWrites.PhysicalIndexOf`.\n  - `ComponentRegistry` indexes the inline fibers of each Portal for the hide path to read. `RestampOwningPortal` keeps the index current when a fiber moves.\n  - `LogicalElementTree.ParentOf` binary-searches.\n- **Range storage.** `PortalRangeStore` replaces the raw range dictionary. It counts ranges per target and caches each target's last end, so `RowsBehindRanges` no longer scans every range for a target that holds none. It also holds the per-target growth a nested patch records, and drops it with the last range on that target.\n- **Nested Portals on one target.** An outer Portal no longer counts an inner same-target Portal's growth in its own length. Removing an inner Portal during the outer's patch nets its length out. The outer recorded a length of 4 for its 2 own rows, and -2 for its 1 row after such a removal.\n- **Detached items.** `ComponentFiber` keeps an append log (`BeginAppendLog`/`EndAppendLog`/`AppendedSince`). `Reconciler.BeginDetachedItemScope` and `StampDetachedItemFibers` read it in place of a snapshot set of every fiber. The Portal drain pairs every `Begin` with an `End`, the throw path included.\n- **Default font family.** `DefaultFamilyRoots.Hold`/`Release` apply to the held subtree only, not to every held root.\n- **Key hashing.** `ChildKey.HashOf` hashes every character. Under Unity's Mono, `string.GetHashCode` stops at the first NUL. `FiberKeying.LeafScope` joins a scope and a key with a NUL, so every key under one keyed wrapper fell into one bucket.\n\n## Evidence\n\nMicroseconds per Portal into one target. Before is the mean of 5 cold runs on the base; after is the mean of 7 warm runs, the first dropped:\n\n| | 250: mount / hide / reveal | 1,000: mount / hide / reveal |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | 587 / 2,136 / ~2,100 | 1,105 / 17,700 / 17,800 |\n| After | 66 / 94 / 73 | 69 / 112 / 79 |\n\nA control with the same number of plain components and no Portals drifts by a similar ~20% on hide (51 to 62).\n\nEach mechanism has a count-based case, red without its fix:\n\n- `PortalRangeStoreTests` (9)\n- `NestedPortalRangeTests`\n- `PortalGrowthEntryTests`\n- `PortalOwnedFiberIndexTests`\n- `ComponentFiberAppendLogTests`\n- `PortalAppendLogReleaseTests`\n- `ChildKeyHashTests`\n- `DefaultFamilyHoldScopeTests`\n\nThe Portal, keyed, Suspense, VirtualList, z-index, `ChildKey`, `DefaultFamily` and `ComponentFiber` EditMode fixtures pass locally: 1,089 passed, none failed or inconclusive.\n\n## Not covered\n\nUnmounting many sibling Portals still scans per Portal. Other string-keyed sets may hold NUL-joined keys. Both are in #1718.\n\nNo `Documentation~` change: no guide describes these costs.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
